Change By:   Antonio Piccolboni <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=piccolbo>

It seems when evaluating a variable in globalenv in a slave process SParkR resolves it to a function by the same name. Renaming the variable is a workaround

{quote}

t = 4
z = 4

SparkR::collect(lapply(parallelize(sc, 1:10), function(x) x > t))

Error in x > t :
  comparison (6) is possible only for atomic and list types
Calls: do.call ... computeFunc -> <Anonymous> -> lapply -> lapply -> FUN
Execution halted
15/02/05 12:13:48 ERROR Executor: Exception in task 0.0 in stage 2.0 (TID 2)
org.apache.spark.SparkException: R computation failed with
 Error in x > t :
  comparison (6) is possible only for atomic and list types

> SparkR::collect(lapply(parallelize(sc, 1:10), function(x) x > z))

[[1]]
[1] FALSE

[[2]]
[1] FALSE

[[3]]
[1] FALSE

[[4]]
[1] FALSE

[[5]]
[1] TRUE

{quote}

