I didn’t realize there is a create-image script.  I’m in the git now, and it seems that the ami’s have not been updated in more than a year.  Perhaps the create image script just needs to be re-run?  Since it seems that you’re the owner of the ec2 script repository, would you work with me on trying to get a working ami?  Looking at the age of these things, I’m starting to wonder if perhaps the issues I’m seeing trying to get spark running, may have to do with the age of the rest of the ami content.  At this point I’ve spent about 15 hours trying to get a 1-master/1-slave cluster with the ec2 scripts to at least pass SparkR run-tests, and no luck.  I recognize that somewhere, someone must be getting this to work, but whomever they are doesn’t seem to be putting their notes online, and its starting to seem easier to build an entire hadoop/spark/etc. installation from scratch.

